{
  "reason": "The current pipeline's complexity (CatBoost + DeepFM + meta-LGBM stacking + target encoding) is mismatched to the 8k-row dataset, as evidenced by the modest 0.7606 accuracy and historical failures of similar high-variance ensembles. Historical successes show that a single well-regularized tree model with native categorical handling, fold-safe OOF threshold tuning, and a fully persisted bundle achieves strong, stable results. Thus the refinement focuses on simplifying to a single tuned LightGBM with native categoricals and seed bagging, while preserving the proven feature engineering and output contract.",
  "module": [
    "data_processing_and_feature_engineering",
    "model_design",
    "training_evaluation"
  ],
  "plan": {
    "data_processing_and_feature_engineering": "WHAT: Modify feature preparation to pass categorical columns directly as pandas category dtype to LightGBM, eliminating integer cat_maps and target encoding from the model matrix; keep CouponFeatureEngineer unchanged and all engineered features. WHY: Historical failures show that target encoding and integer coding impose false ordering and add overfitting risk on small tabular data, while native categorical handling (as in successful CatBoost runs) lets the tree model learn optimal splits without leakage. HOW: In run_training and run_predict, after fe.transform, build a DataFrame where each categorical column is converted to pd.Categorical with categories saved from training (store in bundle as cat_categories_); numeric columns remain as-is. Remove all target encoding calls (_fit_target_encoders, _apply_target_encoders) from the training/predict flow but leave the functions defined for optional use. Preserve function names _prepare_features, _make_lgb_frame, but adapt _make_lgb_frame to accept the category-dtype DataFrame directly. Ensure the saved categories are used at predict time to avoid unseen-category errors, and keep the feature engineer's fitted state (freq maps, etc.) persisted in the bundle.",
    "model_design": "WHAT: Replace the multi-model zoo (DeepFM, CatBoost, meta-LGBM) with a single LightGBM classifier configured for native categorical features, and remove all other model classes and builders. WHY: The initial plan correctly identifies that DeepFM and CatBoost overfit <10k rows, and the meta-stacker amplifies variance from only 3 OOF columns; a single well-regularized LGBM with seed bagging is the empirically strong default for small tabular data, as supported by historical successes with single-model native-categorical approaches. HOW: Keep make_lightgbm but ensure it accepts categorical_feature parameter; remove FocalLoss, DeepFM, _make_cb, make_meta_lgb, and their training/prediction helpers. Optionally tune hyperparameters (e.g., num_leaves=31, min_child_samples=25, learning_rate=0.03) to suit the data size. Preserve the make_lightgbm signature for compatibility, but adjust its arguments if needed to include categorical feature handling. No other model architectures should be instantiated in the final pipeline.",
    "training_evaluation": "WHAT: Rewrite run_training to train a single LightGBM with 5-seed bagging on all training rows, tune threshold on 5-fold OOF predictions (training rows only), and persist a bundle containing the feature engineer, categorical column categories, the 5 LGBM models, threshold, and label map. Rewrite run_predict to load the bundle, transform features using saved state, build the LGBM DataFrame with saved categories, average probabilities from the 5 models, apply the tuned threshold, and output row_id,prediction in original label space. WHY: The initial plan's direction is validated by historical failures of stacking/TE and successes of single-model persisted bundles; seed bagging reduces variance without meta-overfitting, and OOF threshold tuning maintains accuracy alignment. HOW: In run_training, perform 5-fold StratifiedKFold(seed=42) on training rows to compute OOF probabilities using a single LGBM (or one seed per fold), tune threshold on OOF, then train 5 LGBM seeds (0-4) on the full training set. Save all artifacts to a joblib bundle. In run_predict, load the bundle read-only, apply the feature engineer transform (no refit), convert categorical columns to pd.Categorical with saved categories, predict with each of the 5 models, average probabilities, threshold, and map back to original labels. Preserve the output format with row_id = 0..N-1 and original label mapping. Remove any use of target encoding or alternative models in both functions."
  }
}
